      "source": [
        "## 1.3 Weekly return and weekly beta\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1.3.1 Mean weekly return\n",
        "\n",
        "I resampled the daily adjusted close to Friday-ending weeks, taking the last available price in each week.\n",
        "The weekly return is this week's price over last week's minus one. I dropped the first and last weeks of the\n",
        "window because they are incomplete. I kept ordinary holidays, shortened weeks, and did not bridge a missing week.\n",
        "The arithmetic mean of the weekly returns is the return feature."
      ],
      "id": "6Yfvpq1_9A5c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Resample to Friday weeks and take the last price in each week.\n",
        "weekly_prices    = adj_close.resample(\"W-FRI\").last()\n",
        "weekly_benchmark = benchmark_adj.resample(\"W-FRI\").last()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Trim the first and last weeks, which straddle the study boundary and are incomplete.\n",
        "weekly_prices    = weekly_prices.loc[\"2021-01-08\":\"2024-12-27\"]\n",
        "weekly_benchmark = weekly_benchmark.loc[\"2021-01-08\":\"2024-12-27\"]\n",
        "print(\"Weekly observations kept:\", len(weekly_prices))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "nV6-iEhGrSAM",
        "outputId": "e53891a1-0700-4e83-a4fe-a0be886341ae"
      },
      "id": "nV6-iEhGrSAM",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Weekly observations kept: 208\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Weekly returns. fill_method=None means a gap stays a gap instead of being carried forward.\n",
        "weekly_returns    = weekly_prices.pct_change(fill_method=None)\n",
        "benchmark_returns = weekly_benchmark.pct_change(fill_method=None)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Keep only the weeks where the benchmark has a return, so the labels line up for beta.\n",
        "valid_weeks = benchmark_returns.dropna().index\n",
        "weekly_returns    = weekly_returns.loc[valid_weeks]\n",
        "benchmark_returns = benchmark_returns.loc[valid_weeks]\n",
        "print(\"Aligned weekly returns:\", weekly_returns.shape)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
