        "id": "hxRJI5iL9A5c"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 1.3.2 Weekly beta\n",
        "\n",
        "Beta is the covariance of the share's weekly return with the benchmark's, divided by the variance of the\n",
        "benchmark's weekly return, using the full study period. I computed it on the aligned, non-missing weeks\n",
        "only and report how many weeks each beta uses."
      ],
      "id": "hxRJI5iL9A5c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Work out beta share by share, only on weeks where both the share and the market have a return.\n",
        "beta_rows = []\n",
        "for ticker in weekly_returns.columns:\n",
        "    pair = pd.concat([weekly_returns[ticker].rename(\"stock\"),\n",
        "                      benchmark_returns.rename(\"market\")], axis=1).dropna()\n",
        "    n = len(pair)\n",
        "    if n >= 2 and pair[\"market\"].var() > 0:\n",
        "        beta = pair[\"stock\"].cov(pair[\"market\"]) / pair[\"market\"].var()\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        beta = np.nan\n",
        "    beta_rows.append({\"Ticker\": ticker, \"Weekly_Beta\": beta, \"Aligned_Weeks\": n})\n",
        "\n",
        "beta_summary = pd.DataFrame(beta_rows).set_index(\"Ticker\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Bring the return and beta features together into one risk-return table.\n",
        "risk_return = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Mean_Weekly_Return\": mean_weekly_return,\n",
        "    \"Weekly_Beta\": beta_summary[\"Weekly_Beta\"],\n",
        "    \"Aligned_Weeks\": beta_summary[\"Aligned_Weeks\"],\n",
        "})\n",
        "print(\"Aligned weeks range:\", int(risk_return.Aligned_Weeks.min()), \"to\", int(risk_return.Aligned_Weeks.max()))\n",
        "print(risk_return[[\"Mean_Weekly_Return\", \"Weekly_Beta\"]].describe().round(4))"
      ],
