        "## 1.4 Adapted RFM\n",
        "\n",
        "The observation date is the final completed trading session in the window. An unusually high-volume day\n",
        "has volume more than twice the average volume of the previous 20 sessions (I shifted by one day so the day\n",
        "being tested is excluded from its own baseline). I computed the threshold for every share and every day.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Recency**: calendar days from the latest high-volume day to the observation date, missing (never zero) if there is no event.\n",
        "- **Frequency**: number of high-volume days in the last 60 sessions.\n",
        "- **Monetary**: Sum of Close × Volume over the last 60 sessions, in USD."
      ],
      "id": "oHd1Mcpx9A5d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# The observation date is the last session the benchmark trades in the window.\n",
        "observation_date = benchmark_adj.dropna().index.max()\n",
        "# Frequency and Monetary look at the last 60 sessions ending there.\n",
        "last_60_dates = benchmark_adj.dropna().index[-60:]\n",
        "print(\"Observation date:\", observation_date.date())\n",
        "print(\"60-session window:\", last_60_dates.min().date(), \"to\", last_60_dates.max().date())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "tq-IVStKt_E7",
        "outputId": "fab1a8ef-f4d2-450e-80fa-5a667e0e6406"
      },
      "id": "tq-IVStKt_E7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Observation date: 2024-12-31\n",
            "60-session window: 2024-10-07 to 2024-12-31\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Average volume of the PRECEDING 20 sessions: rolling mean, then shift(1) to drop today.\n",
        "avg_volume_20 = volume.rolling(window=20, min_periods=20).mean().shift(1)\n",
        "# A day is a 'high-volume event' if volume is more than twice that preceding average.\n",
        "high_volume_threshold = 2 * avg_volume_20\n",
        "high_volume_events = volume > high_volume_threshold\n",
        "\n",
        "# Quick look at the rule on one share so I can see it is doing the right thing.\n",
        "check = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Volume\": volume[\"AAPL\"],\n",
        "    \"Prev_20_Avg\": avg_volume_20[\"AAPL\"],\n",
