        "# Task 2 — Stock Segmentation and Sensitivity Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2.1 Feature preparation\n",
        "\n",
        "I build two feature matrices and fit two clustering algorithms to each, giving four baseline solutions.\n",
        "Both matrices use the **same common share set** so the comparison is fair: a share needs a valid return,\n",
        "a trustworthy beta (enough aligned weeks) and complete R, F and M. Recency is dropped where there was no\n",
        "event, because the brief says not to substitute zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "Monetary is right-skewed, so I applied `log1p` to it and then standardise each matrix on its own, so no\n",
        "feature dominates the Euclidean distance just because of its units. Recency and Frequency are left in their\n",
        "own units, I show the skew so the decision is visible."
      ],
      "id": "PaUuy2F79A5f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Screening choices (the brief sets no fixed numbers, so I state mine and keep them modest).\n",
        "MIN_ALIGNED_WEEKS = 104   # about two years of weekly history for a stable beta\n",
        "\n",
        "# Shares with usable risk-return features.\n",
        "risk_ok = risk_return[\n",
        "    risk_return[[\"Mean_Weekly_Return\", \"Weekly_Beta\"]].notna().all(axis=1) &\n",
        "    risk_return[\"Aligned_Weeks\"].ge(MIN_ALIGNED_WEEKS)\n",
        "].index\n",
        "\n",
        "# Shares with complete RFM (Recency present means a real event existed).\n",
        "rfm_ok = rfm.dropna(subset=[\"Recency\", \"Frequency\", \"Monetary\"]).index\n",
        "\n",
        "# The common set used for ALL four solutions.\n",
        "common = sorted(set(risk_ok) & set(rfm_ok))\n",
        "print(\"Shares passing risk-return screen:\", len(risk_ok))\n",
        "print(\"Shares with complete RFM:\", len(rfm_ok))\n",
        "print(\"Common shares used everywhere:\", len(common))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Consolidated inclusion / exclusion log (one row per requested ticker, with the reason)\n",
        "exclusion_log = pd.DataFrame(index=tickers)\n",
        "exclusion_log.index.name = \"Ticker\"\n",
        "exclusion_log[\"Available_Days\"] = adj_close.notna().sum().reindex(tickers, fill_value=0)\n",
        "exclusion_log[\"In_Final_Analysis\"] = exclusion_log.index.isin(common)\n",
        "exclusion_log[\"Reason\"] = np.where(\n",
        "    exclusion_log[\"Available_Days\"] == 0, \"no price data\",\n",
        "    np.where(~exclusion_log[\"In_Final_Analysis\"], \"insufficient history / no RFM\", \"retained\"))\n",
        "exclusion_log.to_csv(\"inclusion_exclusion_log.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nInclusion / exclusion summary:\")\n",
        "print(exclusion_log[\"Reason\"].value_counts())\n",
        "exclusion_log.sort_values(\"Available_Days\").head(10)"
      ],
