      "source": [
        "## 2.2 Agglomerative clustering (Ward)\n",
        "\n",
        "Ward linkage with Euclidean distance on the standardised features, one dendrogram per matrix. I compared the\n",
        "cluster count from 2 to 8 on silhouette and cluster sizes, and I read the dendrogram, the\n",
        "coloured branches suggest the natural number of groups, which the silhouette number alone does not settle."
      ],
      "id": "FX221nKw9A5f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Helper: for a matrix, score Ward from k = 2..8 on silhouette and the smallest/largest cluster.\n",
        "def ward_scores(X, name):\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for k in range(2, 9):\n",
        "        labels = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=k, linkage=\"ward\").fit_predict(X)\n",
        "        sizes = pd.Series(labels).value_counts().sort_index()\n",
        "        rows.append({\"Analysis\": name, \"k\": k,\n",
        "                     \"Silhouette\": round(silhouette_score(X, labels), 3),\n",
        "                     \"Smallest\": int(sizes.min()), \"Largest\": int(sizes.max())})\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"k\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ward_risk_scores = ward_scores(X_risk, \"Risk-return\")\n",
        "ward_rfm_scores  = ward_scores(X_rfm, \"RFM\")\n",
        "print(\"Ward_risk_return:\"); display(ward_risk_scores)\n",
        "print(\"Ward_RFM:\"); display(ward_rfm_scores)"
      ],
