      "source": [
        "## 2.3 K-means clustering\n",
        "\n",
        "K-means on the same two matrices, with a fixed seed and 50 initialisations so the result is stable. I\n",
        "compared k = 2..8 on silhouette and inertia (the elbow). The Inertia always falls as k grows, so I read the\n",
        "bend rather than the minimum."
      ],
      "id": "yRJ7SgeS9A5g"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Score K-means from k = 2..8 on silhouette and inertia.\n",
        "def kmeans_scores(X, name):\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for k in range(2, 9):\n",
        "        km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=RANDOM_SEED, n_init=50).fit(X)\n",
        "        sizes = pd.Series(km.labels_).value_counts().sort_index()\n",
        "        rows.append({\"Analysis\": name, \"k\": k,\n",
        "                     \"Silhouette\": round(silhouette_score(X, km.labels_), 3),\n",
        "                     \"Inertia\": round(km.inertia_, 1),\n",
        "                     \"Smallest\": int(sizes.min()), \"Largest\": int(sizes.max())})\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"k\")\n",
        "\n",
        "km_risk_scores = kmeans_scores(X_risk, \"Risk-return\")\n",
        "km_rfm_scores  = kmeans_scores(X_rfm, \"RFM\")\n",
        "print(\"K-means - risk-return:\"); display(km_risk_scores)\n",
        "print(\"K-means - RFM:\"); display(km_rfm_scores)"
