        "## 2.4 Cluster profiles, sector composition and algorithm comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "I included profiles in original units (a return in percent and a traded value in USD mean something, a\n",
        "z-score does not). I compared the two algorithms with the adjusted Rand index, which ignored how the\n",
        "clusters happen to be numbered, and I drew a labelled 2-D PCA view as PCA is only a projection, not a new model."
      ],
      "id": "o1wVQJFu9A5h"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Collect all four solutions and attach sector for the Task 3 analysis.\n",
        "assignments = pd.concat([ward_risk, km_risk, ward_rfm, km_rfm], axis=1)\n",
        "profile_src = risk_feat.join(rfm_feat[[\"Recency\", \"Frequency\", \"Monetary\"]]).join(assignments)\n",
        "profile_src = profile_src.join(sector_lookup[\"GICS Sector\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Original-unit profile for each solution.\n",
        "def show_profile(label, cols):\n",
        "    g = profile_src.groupby(label)\n",
        "    out = g[cols].mean().round(4); out[\"Size\"] = g.size()\n",
        "    print(\"\\nProfile:\", label); display(out)\n",
        "\n",
        "show_profile(\"Ward_Risk\", risk_cols)\n",
        "show_profile(\"KMeans_Risk\", risk_cols)\n",
        "show_profile(\"Ward_RFM\", [\"Recency\", \"Frequency\", \"Monetary\"])\n",
        "show_profile(\"KMeans_RFM\", [\"Recency\", \"Frequency\", \"Monetary\"])"
      ],
